So to decide on a winner.

255
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:43,730
And this is all or nothing because if you get the answer right, you win.

256
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:44,950
If you don't, you lose.

257
00:12:45,290 --> 00:12:47,090
It doesn't matter if you were tied before.

258
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:47,650
Right.

259
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:49,520
All right.

260
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:50,520
A tiebreaker.

261
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:53,570
And we have one more phrase and this one is really interesting.

262
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,310
The pressure is on.

263
00:12:56,470 --> 00:12:58,350
So if I say the pressure is on.

264
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,400
It almost sounds painful.

265
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:01,220
Yeah, it does.

266
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:05,620
Well, is it, does it mean that I am being pressured or what is this?

267
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:06,620
Well, it's a good question.

268
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:17,320
The important thing to look at here is the word on because pressure has this kind of companion word to put pressure on something or to put pressure on someone.

269
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:25,800
And so it's the way we say it in English and it means that you're going to really take things seriously from this point on.

270
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,120
Okay.

271
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:28,120
Right.

272
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:35,080
So for example, the Chicago Bulls were at the peak, the height of their fame and they were just a wonderful team.

273
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:39,880
And oftentimes you'd hear the announcers say, there's five seconds left on the clock.

274
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:43,020
The pressure is on Michael Jordan to win the game.

275
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:43,580
All right.

276
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:48,060
So the opportunity for the team to win all depended on Michael Jordan.

277
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:48,340
Right.

278
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,920
So the pressure, all of this stuff is on him, his shoulders.

279
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:54,720
So he has to score the point to win the game.

280
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,360
Okay.

281
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,480
This is a very interesting phrase.

282
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:02,340
Why don't we take a look at some other examples of how we could use the pressure is on.

283
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:04,490
Example one.

284
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,050
Carl is really stressed out lately.

285
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:14,560
The pressure of the entire project is on him since his promotion.

286
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:16,760
Example two.

287
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:23,200
The pressure is on the president to guide his country out of the recession.

288
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:25,960
Example three.

289
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:33,760
The pressure is on our entire team to successfully come up with a new product for the Asian market within a month.

290
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:33,930
All right.

291
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:35,760
Great examples.

292
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:36,760
Great phrases.

293
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:37,760
I think it's pretty clear now, right?

294
00:14:37,770 --> 00:14:38,110
It is.

295
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:43,350
And to make sure that we understood the whole dialogue, I think we should take another listen to it at a normal speed.

